// clox/string_equality_count.pg -- clox's string_equality.lox made to count:
// == between eight 64-character strings that differ only in the last
// character, 640 a pass, each adding one to a count when true, so none can be
// dropped. The strings are locals swapped in pairs at the end of each pass
// (a1 and a2, a3 and a4, ...), so none can be moved out of the loop; the
// swaps keep every result: 80 are true each pass. The whole loop is timed.
// `count` is the number of passes (clox: 100000). Prints the count, then the
// elapsed ns.

